$  Alice, Bob and Carol each have £10 and want to jointly buy £25 worth of snacks. 
$  Alice has said she will contribute at least as much as Bob, and Carol only has
$  two £5 notes, so will have to contribute a multiple of that. How much should they
$  each contribute?

given combined : int(1..25)
letting individual be 10

$  STEP 1: Add the missing decision variable statement(s) for Alice (a), Bob (b) and Carol (c).
$  The domain for each person will be int(1..10).

(...) : int(1..10)
(...) : int(1..10)
(...) : int(1..10)

$  ASIDE: Try to combine the three statements above into one.


$  STEP 2: Complete the following constraints to satisfy the conditions that the sum will equal
$  the total, that Alice will pay at least as much as Bob and that Carol will pay in multiples
$  of £5.

(...) a + b + c = combined
(...) a >= b
(...) c % 5 = 0

$  ASIDE: Try to combine the three statements above into one.


